 # Madeira Dock
+
+## External executable integration
+
+The parent Madeira integration adds an opt-in external-program adapter. It
+uses the same consumed App-ID-bound native sign-in and Valve subscription-list
+gate as installed games. After genuine client discovery is registered, it
+starts the explicitly selected EXE with `CreateProcessW`, a child-only Steam
+identity, the EXE's working directory and the saved Windows arguments. The
+host pumps the real client's callbacks until the launched job and descendants
+end. No undocumented shortcut interface is added, and neither game libraries
+nor client authentication results are replaced. Installed games retain
+`LaunchApp` and their existing install-directory checks.
+
+The adapter has Windows fixture coverage for Unicode arguments, environment
+isolation, process descendants and error exits. Live authentication and
+external-game compatibility on iOS need device verification. An executable
+that explicitly requests a Steam relaunch can still ask Valve to open the
+installed Steam copy.
 
 Madeira Dock is a headless host for Valve's genuine Steam client, used by the
 Madeira app to launch a user's own purchased games with real Steam
