 # Madeira Dock — implementation handoff, ml2000 (2026-09-25)
+
+## Parent integration: external executable sessions (2026-10-15)
+
+The parent carries `patches/madeira-dock-external-launch.patch` against the
+pinned submodule. `external.c` is reached only from `sh_launch`, after the
+existing genuine sign-in, handoff App ID binding and subscription-list gate.
+Installed launches still use the existing manager ABI and install-directory
+verification. An explicit external launch starts its exact C-drive EXE with
+its own directory/arguments, inherits no handoff path or host launch settings,
+and receives Steam identity only in its child environment. A Windows job
+tracks descendants while the host pumps client callbacks and owns discovery.
+Errors restore discovery through the same cleanup path. No private ABI was
+added. Parent `tests/host/check-external-steam.py` exercises the process adapter
+with synthetic EXEs, not an authenticated Steam session. iOS external-game
+launch and the Wine job-object path remain device test requirements.
 
 ## A manager that answers counts as started (2026-09-29)
 
